om/about-us","name":"Kinaset Therapeutics","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"Kinaset Therapeutics is focused on developing inhaled therapeutics to address significant unmet medical needs in respiratory diseases. Our lead clinical candidate, frevecitinib ( KN-002), is a novel and non-invasive anti-inflammatory to treat all patients with severe asthma."},"country":{"url":"https://eqtgroup.com/news/eqt-life-sciences-backs-kinaset-therapeutics-usd103-million-series-b-to-advance-inhaled-therapeutic-for-treatment-of-respiratory-diseases-2026-01-12","name":"EQT","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-01-12","evidence":"a clinical-stage biopharmaceutical company based in Boston, U.S."},"email":{"url":"https://www.kinasettherapeutics.com/","name":"Kinaset Therapeutics","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"CONTACT info@kinasettx.com 508-858-5810"}},"holding":{"sponsor":"EQT AB","status":"current","status_note":"EQT Life Sciences LSP 7 fund invested in the January 2026 USD 103m Series B","asset_class":"Venture capital","deal_type":"Venture round","value_creation_plan":"Series B proceeds are to help advance frevecitinib, an inhaled pan-JAK inhibitor, through a Phase 2 dose-ranging clinical study in severe asthma; EQT Life Sciences' Daniela Begolo joins Kinaset's board.","value_creation_source_url":"https://eqtgroup.com/news/eqt-life-sciences-backs-kinaset-therapeutics-usd103-million-series-b-to-advance-inhaled-therapeutic-for-treatment-of-respiratory-diseases-2026-01-12","notes":"Round led by RA Capital Management and Forge Life Science Partners, with new investors EQT Life Sciences, Vivo, Schroders, Willett Advisors, Pictet and Sixty Degree Capital, plus existing investors Atlas Venture, 5AM Ventures and Gimv. EQT portfolio page: Fund LSP 7, Entry 2026."}},{"name":"Third Wave Insurance","website":"https://www.thirdwaveinsurance.com","description":"Retail insurance brokerage platform that combines specialized insurance expertise, dedicated agent support and intelligent tec